Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 16:41:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] feat(14-06): wire prometheus_resources.pak into browser
 bundle; real pak-load font/brand tests GREEN (DESIGN-03, DESIGN-05)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires prometheus_resources into the production browser resource bundle:
- chrome/BUILD.gn: packed_resources depends on prometheus_resources and
  merges prometheus_resources.pak into additional_extra_paks.
- chrome/browser/BUILD.gn: browser_resources grit() target depends on
  prometheus_resources so its generated header is reachable tree-wide.
- chrome/browser/prometheus/BUILD.gn: prometheus_unittests gains a data +
  data_deps edge on prometheus_resources_pak so the compiled .pak sits
  next to the test binary at runtime, plus deps on prometheus_resources
  and //ui/base for the resource-bundle test fixture.

Rewrites prometheus_asset_resource_unittest.cc from EXPECT_TRUE(false)
RED stubs to a real pak-load fixture: SetUp() resolves
prometheus_resources.pak via base::PathService::Get(base::DIR_ASSETS)
and loads it with ui::ResourceBundle::AddDataPackFromPath. Each test
asserts BOTH HasDataResource() and GetRawDataResource().size() > 0,
table-driven over all 5 font IDRs and all 7 brand-mark IDRs from
14-ASSET-MANIFEST.md. No static_assert, no uninitialized-bundle check —
GREEN now proves the asset bytes are actually packaged (the HIGH review
finding this plan exists to close). Icon IDR coverage stays owned by
Plan 14-08 per the plan's scope.

Also fixes prometheus_resources.grdp: IDR_PROMETHEUS_ASSET_WORDMARK_DARK/
LIGHT were misnamed against 14-ASSET-MANIFEST.md, which specifies
IDR_PROMETHEUS_ASSET_PM_WORDMARK_DARK/LIGHT (the names the new unittest
table references) — renamed to match the manifest, the authoritative
source of truth for IDR names.

Two build-time defects surfaced only by actually running the test binary
(not just compiling it), fixed here:
1. Include path: the unittest included "grit/prometheus_resources.h",
   but the grd's output_dir = "$root_gen_dir/chrome" means the header
   physically lands at gen/chrome/grit/prometheus_resources.h. Chromium's
   include search root is $root_gen_dir, not $root_gen_dir/chrome, so the
   include needed the chrome/ prefix — confirmed against the identical
   gaia_auth_host_resources.h precedent, which is included elsewhere as
   "chrome/grit/gaia_auth_host_resources.h" with the same output_dir.
2. Test entry point: prometheus_unittests linked //testing/gtest:gtest_main,
   whose bare main() never calls base::CommandLine::Init(). The first real
   ui::ResourceBundle construction in this test suite (SetUp() for the new
   asset-resource fixture) hit ResourceBundle's constructor, which calls
   base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess() and DCHECK-crashed immediately
   at runtime, even though the target compiled and linked cleanly. Swapped
   to //base/test:run_all_unittests (a base::TestSuite-backed main that
   performs the CommandLine/AtExitManager init), matching 15 in-tree
   precedents doing the same swap for the same reason (ui/native_theme,
   crypto, gpu, dbus, among others).

All 15 prometheus_unittests pass (5 asset-resource + 3 action + 4 color
mixer + 2 CSS emission + 1 range check); check-falkon-gpl-guard.sh,
verify-artifact-isolation.sh, and verify-asset-pipeline.sh all clean.
